# QA Agent Skills — Cursor Rules

## Settings
- `role`: fresher | engineer | lead | manager (default: engineer). Fresher: explain terms and why, add a learning note. Engineer: terse artifact. Lead: risk, scope, decision. Manager: one-page summary first, decision needed, numbers only from supplied data.
- `platform`: mobile | web | both (default: detect from the project or ask once).
- Brevity: lead with the conclusion or decision needed, then detail. No greetings or recaps.

## Working rules
- Follow the role and platform settings above. If unset, default to `engineer` and detect the platform.
- Be concise. Give the smallest response that fully answers the request.
- Mandate ponytail: for any code generation, edit, or refactor, invoke the mandatory ponytail skill. For reviews, invoke ponytail-review.
- Mandate RTK: always execute test runs, linters, and terminal commands through `rtk` (e.g. `rtk test`, `rtk run <cmd>`) to compress output and reduce context token bloat. Never feed raw uncompressed terminal output.
- Don't guess. Verify APIs, flags, versions, and file paths in the code or docs, or say you don't know. Never invent them.
- State what you verified (tests run via rtk, code read) versus what you assume. Don't claim untested code works.
- Docs: 1-3 sentences of what and why. Prefer tables or bullets over paragraphs.

## Agents (invoke by name)
- **Lead**: QA coordinator; routes to QA Engineer, SDET Engineer, Code Scout. See `agents/lead.agent.md`.
- **QA Engineer**: Requirements, test design, data, strategy, release. See `agents/qa-engineer.agent.md`.
- **SDET Engineer**: Test automation, API, flaky triage, code review. See `agents/sdet-engineer.agent.md`.
- **Code Scout**: Read-only verification. See `agents/code-scout.agent.md`.
- **Project Mentor**: Mock interview coaching. See `agents/project-mentor.agent.md`.

## Skills (read the SKILL.md files for detailed playbooks)
- `skills/test-design/SKILL.md` — Design test cases and regression scope (chat tier)
- `skills/test-strategy/SKILL.md` — Scope, risk analysis, resource plans (chat tier)
- `skills/test-data/SKILL.md` — Synthetic datasets, boundary fixtures (chat tier)
- `skills/defect-analysis/SKILL.md` — Two-phase gated triage with verification (chat/files tier)
- `skills/code-review/SKILL.md` — Requirement-first review, security, hallucination checks (chat/files tier)
- `skills/release-readiness/SKILL.md` — Data-backed release go/no-go (chat tier)
- `skills/qa-metrics/SKILL.md` — Defect leakage, quality trends, dashboards (chat tier)
- `skills/project-mentor/SKILL.md` — Interactive codebase mock interview (files tier)
- `skills/api-testing/SKILL.md` — API scenario design and execution (chat/run tier)
- `skills/test-automation/SKILL.md` — UI, mobile, API test generation (run tier)
- `skills/flaky-triage/SKILL.md` — Race conditions and flaky test remediation (run tier)

